          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The notion of the exponential modality originates in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+logic"} linear logic
            with
          %ul
            %li#Girard1987
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Linear logic
              %strong 50
              1 (1987) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-3975(87)90045-4"}> doi:10.1016/0304-3975(87)90045-4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://iml.univ-mrs.fr/~girard/linear.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A streamlined statement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            and the observation that these make the exponential a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Seely89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+A.+G.+Seely"}> R. A. G. Seely
                , §2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Linear logic,
                    = succeed "-autonomous" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories in Computer Science and Logic
                %strong 92
                (1989) &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SeelyLinearLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.mcgill.ca/rags/nets/llsac.ps.gz"} ps.gz
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-92"} ISBN:978-0-8218-5100-5
            %li#dePaiva89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"}> Valeria de Paiva
                , §2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Dialectica Categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categories in Computer Science and Logic
                %strong 92
                (1989) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-92"}> ISBN:978-0-8218-5100-5
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/conm/092"} doi:10.1090/conm/092
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anne+Sjerp+Troelstra"}> Anne Sjerp Troelstra
              , §12 in:
              %em Lectures on Linear Logic
              (1992) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://web.stanford.edu/group/cslipublications/cslipublications/site/0937073776.shtml"}> ISBN:0937073776
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Brief survey in a context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+type+theory"} linear type theory
          %ul
            %li{:id => "MihályiNovitzká13"}
              Daniel Mihályi, Valerie Novitzká, Section 2.2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em What about Linear Logic in Computer Science?
              %strong 10
              4 (2013) 147-160 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://acta.uni-obuda.hu/Mihalyi_Novitzka_42.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MihalyiNovitzka-LinearLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Further on the semantics of exponential conjunction as a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
          %ul
            %li#deP1988
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"}> Valeria de Paiva
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Dialectica Categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/techreports/UCAM-CL-TR-213.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/dePaivaDialectica.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#BBP92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Benton"}> Nick Benton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Bierman"} Gavin Bierman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Term assignment for intuitionistic linear logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/techreports/UCAM-CL-TR-262.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BentonBiermanDePaiva-TermAssignment.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (published abridged as
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "#BBPH92"} BBPH92
            %li#BBPH92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Benton"}> Nick Benton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Bierman"} Gavin Bierman
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valeria+de+Paiva"} Valeria de Paiva
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"} Martin Hyland
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Linear
                    = succeed "-Calculus" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi λ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Computer Science Logic. CSL 1992
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 702
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-56992-8_6"} doi:10.1007/3-540-56992-8_6
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (abridged version of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "#BBP92"} BBP92
            %li#BluteCockettSeely96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+F.+Blute"} R. F. Blute
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+R.+B.+Cockett"} J. R. B. Cockett
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+A.+G.+Seely"} R. A. G. Seely
                = succeed "," do
                  %em ! and ? – Storage as tensorial strength
                %strong 6
                4 (1996) 313-351 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129500001055"}> doi:10.1017/S0960129500001055
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#HylandSchalk01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"} Martin Hyland
                and Andreas Schalk,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Glueing and orthogonality for models of linear logic
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.man.ac.uk/~schalk/publ/gomll.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and its
            %a{:href => "monad#CategoryOfAdjunctionResolutionsOfAMonad"} resolution
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+adjunction"} monoidal adjunction
            between the linear and a classical (intuitionistic) type system:
          %ul
            %li#Bierman94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gavin+Bierman"}> Gavin Bierman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Intuitionistic Linear Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Bierman-LinearLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.dropbox.com/s/hdxgubjljb96rmf/Biermanthesis.pdf?dl=0"} pdf
            %li#Benton95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Benton"}> Nick Benton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A mixed linear and non-linear logic: Proofs, terms and models
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Computer Science Logic. CSL 1994
                %strong 933
                (1995) 121-135 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0022251"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0022251
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BentonLinearLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Melliès02"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Andr%C3%A9+Melli%C3%A8s"}> Paul-André Melliès
                ,
                %em Categorical models of linear logic revisited
                (2002) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://hal.science/hal-00154229"}> hal:00154229
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li{:id => "Melliès09"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul-Andr%C3%A9+Melli%C3%A8s"}> Paul-André Melliès
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical semantics of linear logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://smf.emath.fr/publications/modeles-interactifs-de-calcul-et-de-comportement-de-programme"} Interactive models of computation and program behaviour
                %strong 27
                (2009) 1-196 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://smf.emath.fr/publications/semantique-categorielle-de-la-logique-lineaire"}> web
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.irif.fr/~mellies/papers/panorama.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Mellies-CategoricalSemanticsLinear.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Construction of such comonads based on cofree comonoids:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Mellies and Tabareau and Tasson,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em An explicit formula for the free exponential modality of linear logic
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129516000426"} 10.1017/S0960129516000426
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+Slavnov"}> Sergey Slavnov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Banach spaces of sequences and free linear logic exponential modality
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.03853"} arXiv:1509.03853
          %p
            The relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fock+space"} Fock space
            is discussed in:
          %ul
            %li#BlutePanangadenSeely94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Blute"}> Richard Blute
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prakash+Panangaden"} Prakash Panangaden
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+A.+G.+Seely"} R. A. G. Seely
                %em Fock Space: A Model of Linear Exponential Types
                (1994) (
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.27.6825"}> web
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BPSLinear.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Fiore07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Fiore"}> Marcelo Fiore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential Structure in Models of Multiplicative Biadditive Intuitionistic Linear Logic
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~mpf23/papers/Types/diff.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Vicary07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"}> Jamie Vicary
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A categorical framework for the quantum harmonic oscillator
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.0711"} arXiv:0706.0711
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in the context of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory+in+terms+of+dagger-compact+categories"} quantum information theory in terms of dagger-compact categories
          %p
            The interpretation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn ∞
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\infty \Sigma^\infty_+
            as an exponential in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goodwillie+calculus"} Goodwillie calculus
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#AroneKankaanrinta95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Arone"}> Gregory Arone
              , Marja Kankaanrinta,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Goodwillie tower of the identity is a logarithm
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.53.8306"} web
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li#AroneMahowald98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Arone"}> Gregory Arone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Mahowald"} Mark Mahowald
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Goodwillie tower of the identity functor and the unstable periodic homotopy of spheres
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Arone-Mahowald/ArMahowald.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On the
            = succeed "-approach" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            = succeed "-modality:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !
          %ul
            %li#Girard93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
                \.
                %em On the unity of logic
                Annals of Pure and Applied Logic
                %strong 59
                (1993) 201-217 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0168-0072(93)90093-S"}> doi:10.1016/0168-0072(93)90093-S
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Plotkin93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gordon+Plotkin"}> Gordon Plotkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type theory and recursion
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1109/LICS.1993.287571"} doi:10.1109/LICS.1993.287571
            %li#Wadler93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Wadler"}> Philip Wadler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A syntax for linear logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Ninth International Coference on the Mathematical Foundations of Programming Semantics
                %strong 802
                Springer (1993) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-58027-1_24"}> doi:10.1007/3-540-58027-1_24
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#Benton95"} Benton 1995
            %li#Barber96
              %p
                Andrew Barber,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dual Intuitionistic Linear Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/96/ECS-LFCS-96-347/"} web
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/96/ECS-LFCS-96-347/ECS-LFCS-96-347.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barber-DualIntLinLogic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+language"} quantum programming language
            based on this linear/non-linear type theory adunction is
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QWIRE"} QWIRE
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jennifer+Paykin"}> Jennifer Paykin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Rand"} Robert Rand
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Zdancewic"} Steve Zdancewic
              = succeed "," do
                %em QWIRE: a core language for quantum circuits
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/3009837.3009894"} doi:10.1145/3009837.3009894
          %p theoretical background:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jennifer+Paykin"}> Jennifer Paykin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Linear/non-Linear Types For Embedded Domain-Specific Languages
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://repository.upenn.edu/edissertations/2752"} upenn:2752
          %p
            applied to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/verified+programming"} verified programming
            after implementation in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Rand"}> Robert Rand
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jennifer+Paykin"} Jennifer Paykin
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Zdancewic"} Steve Zdancewic
              = succeed "," do
                %em QWIRE Practice: Formal Verification of Quantum Circuits in Coq
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.00699"} arXiv:1803.00699
          %p
            and using ambient
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jennifer+Paykin"}> Jennifer Paykin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Zdancewic"} Steve Zdancewic
              = succeed "," do
                %em A HoTT Quantum Equational Theory
              %a{:href => "http://qpl2019.org/a-hott-quantum-equational-theory/"} talk at QPL2019
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.04371"}> arXiv:1904.04371
              )
          %p
            The !-modality in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+logic"} affine logic
            applied to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %ul
            %li#Shulman2022
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Affine logic for constructive mathematics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/bsl.2022.28"} doi:10.1017/bsl.2022.28
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.07518"} arXiv:1805.07518
          %h3#in_dependent_linear_type_theory In dependent linear type theory
          %p
            Discussion of the exponential modality via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+homotopy+type+theory"} dependent linear homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#PontoShulman12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kate+Ponto"}> Kate Ponto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Duality and traces in indexed monoidal categories
                %strong 26
                23 (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.1555"}> arXiv:1211.1555
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/23/26-23abs.html"} tac:26-23
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2011/11/traces_in_indexed_monoidal_cat.html"} blog
            %li#Schreiber14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                , Sec. 4.2 of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Quantization+via+Linear+homotopy+types"} Quantization via Linear homotopy types
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1402.7041"}> arXiv:1402.7041
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Riley22Thesis
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mitchell+Riley"}> Mitchell Riley
                , §2.1.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Bunched Homotopy Type Theory for Synthetic Stable Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.14418/wes01.3.139"} doi:10.14418/wes01.3.139
          %p
            The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\infty \Sigma^\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic+functor"} comonadicity
            of simply connected pointed spaces over spectra:
          %ul
            %li#BlomquistHarper16
              %p
                Jacobson R. Blomquist, John E. Harper, Thm. 1.8 in:
                %em Suspension spectra and higher stabilization
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.08623"}> arXiv:1612.08623
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#HessKedziorek17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magdalena+Kedziorek"} Magdalena Kedziorek
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The homotopy theory of coalgebras over simplicial comonads
                %strong 21
                1 (2019) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.07104"}> arXiv:1707.07104
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2019.v21.n1.a11"} doi:10.4310/HHA.2019.v21.n1.a11
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/logic"} logic
